- op: discuss  # 8263
  at: '2026-06-21T01:51:52Z'  # 8263
  by: agent  # 8263
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 8263
  clock: 6  # 8263
  nonce: '8263'  # 8263
  message: "Done — merged as PR #4251 (origin/dev a98bb7a6af). Implemented BOTH desync recoveries (human-approved 'auto-pr without --gov', scope 'both push + merge'): (1) do_pr AGit-push fallback -> plain non-force branch push + API create_pr (new in forgejo-api.sh), reusing any partial-AGit PR (+ re-check after a non-2xx create_pr to avoid a duplicate vPR) before queueing a vPR; (2) do_merge resync-retry -> on a final-attempt desync-signature failure (405/000/5xx/proc-receive/try-again), one plain branch push to resync the DB + one merge retry, verified via EITHER the PR record OR git ground truth (_pr_landed_in_base / git merge-base --is-ancestor). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: 22 production-path tests in tests/test_autopr_desync_fallback.py exercise the real bash funcs via 'source forgejo-api.sh' + subprocess auto-pr runs — create_pr (seam + mocked-api payload/number extraction + failure), _merge_failure_is_desync matrix (405/000/body=desync; 200/422=not), _attempt_desync_resync_push seam, do_merge resync recover-via-git-when-PR-flag-lags / give-up-when-not-landed / no-resync-on-422, and the full auto-pr fallback flow (create-PR-no-vPR vs branch-push-fail->vPR); 41 existing auto-pr/merge-pr tests still green. Adversarially reviewed (4-dimension review workflow + per-finding verify): 8 real findings; the HIGH (resync-retry originally verified via the lagging PR 'merged' flag, which would MISS the FF-landed 'reports-failure-but-succeeds' case it targets — the #4247 scenario) was fixed before merge via the _pr_landed_in_base git-ancestor check. Dogfood: PR #4251 itself merged via the new do_merge FF path (clean, no desync this run). Branch pushes are non-force and never target a protected branch. Note: flush_queue's AGit push was left without the fallback (do_pr-only scope); a follow-up could extend it."  # 8263
